('HRM', 'Human Resource Management', 'HRM.7', 'There is a process for credentialing and privileging of medical professionals, permitted to provide patient care without supervision.', 'HRM.7.d', 'Commitment', 'The requisite services to be provided by the medical professionals are known to them as well as the various departments/units of the organisation.'),
('HRM', 'Human Resource Management', 'HRM.8', 'There is a process for credentialing and privileging of nursing professionals, permitted to provide patient care without supervision', 'HRM.8.a', 'Core', 'Nursing staff permitted by law, regulation and the organisation to provide patient care without supervision are identified.'),
('HRM', 'Human Resource Management', 'HRM.8', 'There is a process for credentialing and privileging of nursing professionals, permitted to provide patient care without supervision', 'HRM.8.b', 'Commitment', 'The education, registration, training, experience and other information of nursing staff are identified, verified, documented and updated periodically.'),
('HRM', 'Human Resource Management', 'HRM.8', 'There is a process for credentialing and privileging of nursing professionals, permitted to provide patient care without supervision', 'HRM.8.c', 'Core', 'Nursing staff are granted privileges in consonance with their qualification, training, experience and registration'),
('HRM', 'Human Resource Management', 'HRM.8', 'There is a process for credentialing and privileging of nursing professionals, permitted to provide patient care without supervision', 'HRM.8.d', 'Commitment', 'The requisite services to be provided by the nursing staff are known to them as well as the various departments/units of the organisation.'),
('HRM', 'Human Resource Management', 'HRM.9', 'There is a process for credentialing and privileging of para-clinical professionals, permitted to provide patient care without supervision.', 'HRM.9.a', 'Core', 'Para-clinical professionals permitted by law, regulation and the organisation to provide patient care without supervision are identified'),
