('HRM', 'Human Resource Management', 'HRM.9', 'There is a process for credentialing and privileging of para-clinical professionals, permitted to provide patient care without supervision.', 'HRM.9.c', 'Core', 'Para-clinical professionals are granted privileges in consonance with their qualification, training, experience and registration.'),
('HRM', 'Human Resource Management', 'HRM.9', 'There is a process for credentialing and privileging of para-clinical professionals, permitted to provide patient care without supervision.', 'HRM.9.d', 'Commitment', 'The requisite services to be provided by the para-clinical professionals are known to them as well as the various departments/units of the organisation.'),
('IMS', 'Information Management System', 'IMS.1', 'Information needs of the stakeholders are met and data is captured and analyzed appropriately', 'IMS.1.a', 'Core', 'The organization identifies, captures and disseminates the information needs of the patients, visitors, staff, management, external agencies and community.'),
('IMS', 'Information Management System', 'IMS.1', 'Information needs of the stakeholders are met and data is captured and analyzed appropriately', 'IMS.1.b', 'Commitment', 'Information management and technology acquisitions and maintenance plan are in consonance with the identified information needs.'),
('IMS', 'Information Management System', 'IMS.1', 'Information needs of the stakeholders are met and data is captured and analyzed appropriately', 'IMS.1.c', 'Commitment', 'The organisation stores and retrieves data according to its information needs.'),
('IMS', 'Information Management System', 'IMS.1', 'Information needs of the stakeholders are met and data is captured and analyzed appropriately', 'IMS.1.d', 'Commitment', 'The organization contributes to external databases in accordance with the law and regulations.'),
('IMS', 'Information Management System', 'IMS.1', 'Information needs of the stakeholders are met and data is captured and analyzed appropriately', 'IMS.1.e', 'Commitment', 'Processes for data collection are standardized and data is analysed to meet the information needs.'),
('IMS', 'Information Management System', 'IMS.2', 'The patients cared for by the organisation have a complete and accurate medical record.', 'IMS.2.a', 'Core', 'The unique identifier is assigned to the medical record'),
('IMS', 'Information Management System', 'IMS.2', 'The patients cared for by the organisation have a complete and accurate medical record.', 'IMS.2.b', 'Core', 'The contents of medical record are identified, documented and provides a complete, up-to-date and chronological account of patient care.'),
('IMS', 'Information Management System', 'IMS.2', 'The patients cared for by the organisation have a complete and accurate medical record.', 'IMS.2.c', 'Commitment', 'Authorized staff make the entry in the medical record, author of the entry can be identified.'),
('IMS', 'Information Management System', 'IMS.2', 'The patients cared for by the organisation have a complete and accurate medical record.', 'IMS.2.d', 'Commitment', 'Entry in the medical record is named, signed, dated and timed.'),
('IMS', 'Information Management System', 'IMS.2', 'The patients cared for by the organisation have a complete and accurate medical record.', 'IMS.2.e', 'Commitment', 'The medical record has only authorised abbreviations.'),
('IMS', 'Information Management System', 'IMS.3', 'The medical record reflects the continuity of care.', 'IMS.3.a', 'Commitment', 'The medical record contains information regarding reasons for admission, diagnosis and plan of care.'),
('IMS', 'Information Management System', 'IMS.3', 'The medical record reflects the continuity of care.', 'IMS.3.b', 'Commitment', 'The medical record contains the details of assessments, re-assessments, consultations, results of investigations, operative and other procedures, and the details of the care provided.'),
('IMS', 'Information Management System', 'IMS.3', 'The medical record reflects the continuity of care.', 'IMS.3.c', 'Commitment', 'When patient is transferred to another hospital, the medical record contains the details of the transfer.'),
